## 4. Belhaven Faculty Response Protocol (Elevated Detection Scores)

Faculty must independently evaluate student work before viewing detection scores. If elevated scores coincide with writing inconsistencies, faculty follow a structured response workflow:

```text
[Independent Paper Review] ---> [Concerns + High Score] ---> [Evaluate Syllabus Permissions]
                                                                    |
               +----------------------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------+
               |                                                                                                         |
               v                                                                                                         v
  [Assignments Permitting AI]                                                                               [Assignments Prohibiting AI]
  * Option 1: Informational Notice                                                                          * Option A: Reminder & Clarification
  * Option 2: Request Evidence of Learning (Drafts/Notes)                                                   * Option B: Opportunity to Demonstrate Learning
  * Option 3: Conversation Invitation (Oral Defense)                                                        * Option C: Confirmed Misconduct Referral
  * Option 4: Revision & Reflection Opportunity
  * Option 5: Academic Integrity Process Referral
